meta {
  name: List categories
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/categories
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  page: 1
  limit: 10
  ~sort: id
  ~order: desc
  ~search: a
}

docs {
  # List categories

  Product categories the storefront and the mobile app filter by. `code` doubles as the URL slug.

  Returns one page of active categories. Soft-deleted records never appear.

  ## Auth

  None. Public.

  ## Query parameters

  | Name | Type | Required | Notes |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `page` | integer | no | 1-based page; default 1. A page past the end returns `data: []` with correct `pagination`. |
  | `limit` | integer | no | Page size; default 10; values above 100 are clamped to 100. |
  | `sort` | string | no | One of: id, name, code, createdAt. Default `id`. |
  | `order` | string | no | `asc` or `desc`; default `desc`. |
  | `search` | string | no | Case-insensitive match against: name, code. |

  ## Responses

  ### 200 OK

    {
      "message": "Category list",
      "data": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "name": "Garden",
          "code": "garden",
          "img": "https://picsum.photos/seed/lpa-garden/640/640",
          "description": "Garden gear from Lpaecomms.",
          "created": {
            "client": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
            "server": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
            "serverDate": "2026-09-27",
            "serverTime": "12:30:14",
            "unixTime": 1790476214,
            "user": 1,
            "role": "ADMIN"
          },
          "updated": null,
          "statusName": "ACTIVE",
          "status": 1,
          "createdAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z",
          "updatedAt": "2026-09-27T02:30:14.000Z"
        }
      ],
      "pagination": {
        "total": 1,
        "page": 1,
        "limit": 10,
        "totalPages": 1,
        "count": 1,
        "hasNextPage": false,
        "hasPrevPage": false
      }
    }

  ### 400 Bad Request — validation failed

  A paging, sort or filter parameter is invalid (e.g. `page=0`, an unknown `sort`).

    {
      "message": "Some fields need attention.",
      "data": null,
      "pagination": null,
      "errors": [
        {
          "field": "page",
          "message": "Invalid input"
        }
      ]
    }

  Outside production, error bodies also carry `stack`.
}
